      "speaker": null,
      "text": "THE SECOND AORIST",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 7,
      "bbox": [
        467,
        195,
        518,
        901
      ],
      "margin_number": 144,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "As we earlier warned (129), a number of verbs do not form their aorists on\nthe pattern of what we have called first aorist (basically, present stem + -σα)\nbut on the pattern of what is called second aorist (or 'strong aorist').",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 8,
      "bbox": [
        521,
        246,
        539,
        747
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "Note carefully the following about second aorist forms:",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "box",
      "order": 9,
      "bbox": [
        551,
        93,
        667,
        915
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "► They have an aorist stem different from that of the present:\n► For example, the aorist stem of λαμβάνω, 'I take', is λαβ-, and that of\nγίγνομαι, 'I become', is γεν- ;\n► They form the strong aorist indicative by adding the augment to this\nstem in the usual way, ἐ-λαβ-, ἐ-γεν-, to indicate that the action is\npast.\n► They have personal endings different from first aorist endings (no\n-σα).",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": "black_right_pointing_pointer",
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
